# docs/calibration/CAL-007-PROVISIONAL.log — @pixagram/paph-x 1.2.0
#
# CAL-007-PROVISIONAL, comparator 42's calibration from 1.2: CAL-004-PROPOSED with the moderate
# structural bar (thresholds[2]) at 3300. Quoted by docs/SPEC-004.2-paph-v42.md §19, the CHANGELOG,
# docs/PAPH-X.md §4, docs/SPEC-SI-paph-si.md §11, docs/SEARCH.md §4 and the integration's README.
# Native, one core of a shared two-core container (Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.10GHz), rustc 1.97.0;
# rust/target/release/{sibench,xbench,xcli}, run from rust/; Node 22.22 for the test/ and tools/ scripts,
# run from the repository root. Counts, classes, recalls and artefacts are deterministic and reproduce
# exactly from the same snapshot; timings move by a few per cent between runs, and more when the host is
# busy.
#
# The snapshot is 1.1.2's (docs/calibration/SI3-PROVISIONAL.log, run 0): rust/target/chain-corpus,
# head block 987642, manifest sha256 8d06cb4711e0e1e9c43dabe50edf3ed11039975a17dbc9bfec0afcf1dd27c055.
# The images are not in the repository; no author or permlink appears in the output.
#
# Runs 1 and 2 hash both corpora in wire 4 (docs/SPEC-W4-paph-wire4.md); every later run here, in
# X3-PROVISIONAL.log and in SI4-PROVISIONAL.log reads those caches. Run 3 fits the bar on the chain's
# pairs of two authors' works and shows what it moves on the chain, its real-base corpus and the
# synthetic corpus; without --out it writes docs/calibration/CAL-007-PROVISIONAL.pcal — here a copy,
# and the sha256 lines at the end show it equal to the committed file. Run 4 snapshots every pair's
# lattice inputs (TSV under rust/target/calib) and run 5 recomputes the lattice on them, under
# CAL-004 (which must reproduce the verdict each row recorded) and under CAL-007.

